    "udt_error_enum_v0": {
      "doc": "",
      "lib": "",
      "name": "Error",
      "cases": [
        {
          "doc": "`tokens` or `engine` passed into `create_engine`/`create_pool_and_escrow` is not the\\nexact value `salt` actually deployed in an earlier phase (see the module doc's\\n\"Determinism\" section). Catches a wrong `salt` or a stale/copy-pasted struct *before* any\\none-time wiring (`set_minter`, `set_recovery_escrow`) is consumed irreversibly against the\\nwrong contract -- found during an audit review: nothing previously checked this on-chain,\\neven though `predict_market` could trivially recompute and assert the same addresses.\\n\\nThis proves `tokens`/`engine` is salt-arithmetic-consistent -- the one value derivable\\nfrom `salt` -- not that the earlier phase was actually run for this `salt` (the address\\nderivation is a pure function of `salt` alone, independent of whether anything is\\ndeployed there; confirmed via a final audit review). Skipping a phase entirely is still\\ncaught, just by a different mechanism: every real wiring call this function makes right\\nafter (`set_minter`, `set_risk_control`, `set_recovery_escrow`, ...) ",
          "name": "TopologyMismatch",
          "value": 1
        }
      ]
    }
  },
